    "message": "Drop kept restored worlds once no read used them for a minute\n\nA kept copy shares its EventLog records with the restored world, so it\nholds about 140 MiB of Python objects for a 1440-minute world. The local\nserver now drops the kept copies 60 seconds after the last read that used\nthem and collects once, instead of holding them until two other\nCheckpoints are read.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
